Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Build a Large Language Model from Scratch \[LongDash] in Wolfram Language\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"c92a9806-1132-47e7-81c8-7394b43ce96a"],

Cell["Part 7: Reinforcement learning post-training (GRPO)", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"8b7491fe-b421-4a9e-b977-ddda155b1ad4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Supervised fine-tuning in Part 6 made the model do question-and-",
 "answer. RL post-training is the next step: take the SFT model, sample ",
 "completions on a task with a verifiable reward, and update the policy ",
 "to make high-reward completions more likely. Following nanochat, we ",
 "use ",
 StyleBox["GRPO",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " in its simplest form \[LongDash] no reference model, no KL term, ",
 "centered advantages over a group of rollouts."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e0fc5eb-1511-43a8-9926-0f2a790c071b"],

Cell["1.  Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e5700cae-abd3-48c7-bedd-751c4213d78e"],

Cell["SetDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"15aa198b-cdc8-45cc-bb78-d739b83d5068"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"../../part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/src/Tokeniser.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-02-self-attention/src/Attention.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-03-transformer-block/src/Transformer.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-04-pretraining/src/Training.wl\"]
Get[\"../../part-05-sampling/src/Sampling.wl\"]
Get[\"src/RL.wl\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a9d36d3f-6721-40c5-9d2e-de87f0648d07"],

Cell["2.  The GRPO recipe in five lines", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"14b74f2b-fbb8-4d11-8569-130849958b12"],

Cell["Per training step, given a prompt:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2632289c-1981-4657-a7f4-824a46b98637"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "1. ",
 StyleBox["Sample",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData["K"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"99978ee6-40a8-49e3-bf00-168735e9886f"],
 " rollouts at temperature ",
 Cell[BoxData["T"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"88abe9cf-c426-4a22-8281-9f4e72daddda"],
 " from the current policy.\n",
 "2. ",
 StyleBox["Score",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " each rollout with a reward function ",
 Cell[BoxData["R"], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"8d5dc66c-6174-490d-a886-15f9a80d68e0"],
 " (binary for verifiable tasks).\n",
 "3. ",
 StyleBox["Center",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " the rewards: advantages = rewards \[LongDash] mean(rewards).\n",
 "4. ",
 StyleBox["Compute",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " policy-gradient loss ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"L", "=", "-", "\[Sum]"}]], "Text",
  FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"9ab6288b-2c39-45b0-be78-f32a2e768339"],
 " advantage_i \[CenterDot] log p_\[Theta](rollout_i).\n",
 "5. ",
 StyleBox["Step",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ADAM on L."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ee447d0-f73b-4613-b09e-7c2b2065d5f3"],

Cell["\<\
What's deliberately absent: no reference model, no KL divergence, no value \
head, no importance-weighting. The reward IS the ground truth, the variance \
across the K rollouts IS the advantage signal. It is shocking how simple this \
is once you accept that you don't need PPO's machinery for tasks with \
verifiable correctness.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c9b047dd-d620-45f4-9f7e-f2a3c876cbc4"],

Cell["3.  A verifiable toy task: end with <|eot|>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"429d5750-985e-4991-9a4f-6b029df9fbf5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the educational demo we use the trivial task ",
 StyleBox["\"end your continuation with the <|eot|> token within k tokens\"",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ". Binary reward: 1.0 if the rollout contains <|eot|>, else 0.0. ",
 "Small models post-trained from random init learn to do this in a few ",
 "minutes of CPU time, while preserving all the GRPO bookkeeping that ",
 "scales to real verifiable tasks (GSM8K, code, format-following)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"49847268-ceca-4f81-abb3-1b4114e2e86b"],

Cell["4.  One full GRPO step, walked through", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"10797c72-1ec5-4f3c-865f-ac745f22cbb8"],

Cell["\<\
(* Pretend we have the SFT model from Part 6.  For the demo we
     just use a fresh small model so the notebook runs standalone. *)
SeedRandom[1];
bpe = Import[\"../../part-01-tokeniser-and-embeddings/data/bpe_trained.mx\"];
baseVocab = LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`buildBPEVocabulary[bpe];
chatVocab = Join[baseVocab, {\"<|user|>\", \"<|assistant|>\", \"<|eot|>\"}];
tokId = AssociationThread[chatVocab -> Range[Length[chatVocab]]];
net = LLMAtoZ`Transformer`gptModel[64, 4, 2, 128, Length[chatVocab], 64];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"8ccb77f5-2d27-417c-8495-44b73924c9da"],

Cell["\<\
promptIds = Lookup[tokId,
  LLMAtoZ`Tokeniser`bpeEncode[\"ROMEO:\", bpe[\"MergeRules\"]]];
rollouts = LLMAtoZ`RL`rolloutBatch[net, promptIds, 8, 24, 64, 1.0];
rewards = Map[LLMAtoZ`RL`rewardEot[#, tokId[\"<|eot|>\"]] &, rollouts];
{Length[rollouts], rewards}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d12bd5ff-f2e2-40bf-bf5c-b58d2f0e2d76"],

Cell["\<\
advantages = LLMAtoZ`RL`centerAdvantages[rewards];
advantages\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"395a5cad-1383-4cf6-bad0-0216af918346"],

Cell["5.  Run a small GRPO epoch", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e6632a39-e786-4b40-bd79-d5b5f0555c9f"],

Cell["\<\
prompts = LLMAtoZ`RL`toyPromptSet[bpe[\"MergeRules\"], tokId];
hp = <|\"NRollouts\" -> 6, \"GenerationLen\" -> 20,
       \"Temperature\" -> 1.2, \"LearningRate\" -> 0.001,
       \"ContextLen\" -> 64, \"EotId\" -> tokId[\"<|eot|>\"]|>;
res = LLMAtoZ`RL`runGrpoEpoch[net, prompts, hp];
Length[res[\"History\"]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"67cfb9c8-7a0b-45d8-ac55-69d93a84f2e0"],

Cell["\<\
ListLinePlot[
  res[\"History\"][[All, \"meanReward\"]],
  Frame -> True,
  FrameLabel -> {\"step\", \"mean reward over the rollout group\"},
  PlotLabel -> \"GRPO learning curve on the EOT-ending task\",
  PlotStyle -> Directive[ColorData[97][1], Thick],
  ImageSize -> 540, GridLines -> Automatic]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6f6d7b08-8171-479b-be34-51cc976549dc"],

Cell["6.  Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"89973284-62f0-44dc-b5f1-221d6f3cd280"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["A full GRPO loop in less than 100 lines.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " ",
 StyleBox["rolloutBatch",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["centerAdvantages",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["policyGradientStep",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["runGrpoEpoch",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " \[LongDash] no ",
 "reference model, no KL term, no value head, no PPO clipping.\n",
 "\[FilledSquare] ",
 StyleBox["A trivial verifiable task",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " (end-with-EOT) that exercises every step of the loop while ",
 "finishing in minutes of CPU time. The same code with a different ",
 StyleBox["rewardFn",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " trains on GSM8K \[LongDash] swap one function."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f3326079-21d8-479d-a9c6-c551ad091bd6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In ",
 StyleBox["Part 8",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " we put the post-trained model behind an interactive chat widget ",
 "inside the notebook \[LongDash] the final artefact of the series."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ba8fff4c-a1e0-4002-9a55-cb8b7d87ae71"],

Cell["References", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a2173b89-4a06-439a-9721-b3274fd33b17"],

Cell["\<\
Shao, Z. et al. (2024). DeepSeekMath: Pushing the Limits of Mathematical \
Reasoning in Open Language Models. (GRPO.)
Yu, F. et al. (2024). DAPO: An Open-Source LLM Reinforcement Learning System \
at Scale.
Karpathy, A. (2025). nanochat.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"189c6b51-1ea8-4b02-8754-d035d875b034"]
},
